 "capsule": "Makuria emerged as a Christian Nubian kingdom centered on Dongola in the Nile's Dongola Reach, converting from Nubian traditional religion to Christianity around the mid-6th century under Byzantine missionary influence. It became the dominant power of medieval Nubia, later absorbing the neighboring kingdom of Nobadia and holding off Arab-Egyptian invasions after negotiating the Baqt treaty (c. 652). Makuria's central authority weathered internal succession disputes and periodic Mamluk incursions until dynastic collapse and civil war in the early 14th century eroded its power, though a much-reduced kingdom persisted at Dongola into the 15th century.",
